# Glossary (spec §12.1, §12.3): every term a lesson lists in `glossary` has
# `glossary-<id>` (the term) and `glossary-<id>-def` (the definition) here.

glossary-alpha = Alpha
glossary-alpha-def = How often a bluff must make the opponent fold to break even: bet / (pot + bet).
glossary-barrel = Barrel
glossary-barrel-def = A bet on a later street after betting the previous one: the turn bet after a flop c-bet is the second barrel.
glossary-big-blind = Big blind (bb)
glossary-big-blind-def = The larger forced bet, and the unit Taful measures stacks and pots in.
glossary-blocker = Blocker
glossary-blocker-def = A card you hold that removes combos from your opponent's range.
glossary-bluff = Bluff
glossary-bluff-def = A bet made to fold better hands, with a hand that rarely wins at showdown.
glossary-bluff-catcher = Bluff-catcher
glossary-bluff-catcher-def = A hand that beats only the opponent's bluffs and loses to every value bet.
glossary-board = Board
glossary-board-def = The community cards every player shares: flop, turn and river.
glossary-button = Button (BTN)
glossary-button-def = The dealer seat. It acts last after the flop, the best position at the table.
glossary-c-bet = Continuation bet (c-bet)
glossary-c-bet-def = A flop bet by the player who made the last raise before the flop.
glossary-check-raise = Check-raise
glossary-check-raise-def = Checking, then raising after the opponent bets.
glossary-cold-call = Cold call
glossary-cold-call-def = Calling a raise before the flop without having put chips in voluntarily first.
glossary-combo = Combo
glossary-combo-def = One exact two-card combination, such as A♠ K♠. AKs has 4, AKo 12, a pair 6.
glossary-dirty-outs = Dirty outs
glossary-dirty-outs-def = Cards that complete your draw but also improve your opponent to a better hand.
glossary-effective-stack = Effective stack
glossary-effective-stack-def = The smaller of the two stacks in a hand: the most either player can win or lose.
glossary-equity = Equity
glossary-equity-def = Your share of the pot if all cards were dealt with no more betting.
glossary-ev = Expected value (EV)
glossary-ev-def = What a decision wins or loses on average: the sum of each outcome times its probability.
glossary-exploit = Exploit
glossary-exploit-def = A deliberate move away from the reference strategy to win more from an opponent's mistake.
glossary-fold-equity = Fold equity
glossary-fold-equity-def = The value a bet gains from the times the opponent folds.
glossary-four-bet = 4-bet
glossary-four-bet-def = The re-raise after a 3-bet before the flop.
glossary-gto = Game-theory optimal (GTO)
glossary-gto-def = An equilibrium strategy: neither player can gain by changing their play alone.
glossary-implied-odds = Implied odds
glossary-implied-odds-def = Pot odds plus the chips you expect to win on later streets when you hit.
glossary-kicker = Kicker
glossary-kicker-def = A side card that breaks ties between hands of the same category.
glossary-leak = Leak
glossary-leak-def = A group of similar spots where you keep losing EV.
glossary-linear = Linear range
glossary-linear-def = A range built top-down: the best hands take the action, and the rest do something else.
glossary-mdf = Minimum defense frequency (MDF)
glossary-mdf-def = How often you must continue against a bet so bluffs do not profit automatically: pot / (pot + bet).
glossary-multiway = Multiway pot
glossary-multiway-def = A pot with three or more players after the flop.
glossary-nut-advantage = Nut advantage
glossary-nut-advantage-def = Having more of the strongest possible hands on a board than the opponent.
glossary-outs = Outs
glossary-outs-def = Cards that, if they come next, put you ahead.
glossary-polarized = Polarized range
glossary-polarized-def = A range of very strong hands and bluffs, with few medium hands.
glossary-position = Position
glossary-position-def = Acting after your opponent on a street. The player in position sees more before deciding.
glossary-pot-odds = Pot odds
glossary-pot-odds-def = The equity a call needs to break even: bet / (pot + 2 × bet).
glossary-range = Range
glossary-range-def = The set of hands a player can hold in a spot, with how often each is played.
glossary-range-advantage = Range advantage
glossary-range-advantage-def = Having more equity with your whole range on a board than the opponent has with theirs.
glossary-rfi = Open raise (RFI)
glossary-rfi-def = The first raise before the flop when everyone before you folded: raise first in.
glossary-semi-bluff = Semi-bluff
glossary-semi-bluff-def = A bet with a hand that is behind now but can improve to the best hand.
glossary-showdown-value = Showdown value
glossary-showdown-value-def = A hand's chance to win if the hand is checked down to showdown.
glossary-spr = Stack-to-pot ratio (SPR)
glossary-spr-def = Effective stack divided by the pot on the flop; how committed the hand is.
glossary-squeeze = Squeeze
glossary-squeeze-def = A 3-bet after an open raise and one or more calls.
glossary-texture = Board texture
glossary-texture-def = How a board's height, suits, connections and pairs shape both ranges.
glossary-thin-value = Thin value
glossary-thin-value-def = A value bet with a hand only slightly ahead of the hands that call.
glossary-three-bet = 3-bet
glossary-three-bet-def = The first re-raise before the flop (the big blind counts as the first bet).
glossary-tilt = Tilt
glossary-tilt-def = Playing worse because of emotions such as frustration after a loss.
glossary-value-bet = Value bet
glossary-value-bet-def = A bet made to get called by worse hands.
glossary-variance = Variance
glossary-variance-def = How far short-term results swing around their expected value.
